WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.136
-Republicans have spent
the last few days

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:06.472
spreading the baseless claim
that mass cancelations

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.341
and delays
by Southwest Airlines

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.642
were due to President Biden's

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.277
vaccine and testing
requirements.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.479
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:17.750 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.386
There was a big milestone today
in the pandemic,

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.889
19 months after the U.S.
closed its borders

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.792
to the north and south,
they're opening back up again.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.995
-The U.S. set to announce plans
to reopen the borders

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.232
with Canada and Mexico,
but only to certain travelers.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:35.635
-This morning America is
signaling it's open for business

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.670
from across the border again.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.573
The White House says
it will lift a 19 month ban

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.543
for foreign travelers
crossing land borders

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.845
from both Canada and Mexico,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:50.150
but only for visitors who can
prove they're fully vaccinated.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.719
-Huge news for tourists,
migrants, and the one guy

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.188
who was on spring break
in Cancun in March 2020

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.156
and didn't make it
back out in time.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:58.591
"Hey, it's me, Brad.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.993
Hey, can you forward
my mail to Señor --

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.896
What was your last name again?
Frog's?

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.965
No, it's not the bar!
It's also a popular last name!

00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:09.802
Just forward my mail!

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.871
And I, for one,
miss Canadian tourists.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:12.972
They were so polite.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.374
If one was standing
in Times Square,

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.674
takin' up the whole sidewalk

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.544
with their giant ass
goose down coats.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.712
You could just give them
a big ol' shove

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.816
and they'd apologize to you!

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:26.585
"Oh, sorry for goosin'
the sidewalk, eh?

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:29.222
I just never seen
so many Legos."

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.524
So tourism is starting
to come back.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.160
Although I will say one of
the many strange things

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.562
about lockdown life
is that after a year

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:38.464
of not going anywhere,
I forgot how to travel.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.900
You know how, in the old days,
you'd be kind of bummed

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.336
if your Uber driver wanted to
make small talk the whole time.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.837
Now it's the other way around --

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.072
the Uber driver is annoyed

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.140
because I won't stop
talking to them.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.176
"So where are you from?!"

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.511
"Uh, you know, around."
"You like driving?!"

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.748
"Yeah. Sor-- I just can't hear
you with the mask on."

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:59.018
"But the mask doesn't
cover your ears.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:02.955
We had audiences back
this week!"

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.289
I've com--

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:08.294
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.096
I've completely, completely
forgotten how to pack

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:13.732
for vacations: the first time
I flew post-lockdown,

00:02:13.732 --> 00:02:15.401
TSA did a check
in my suitcase

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.302
and found 10 pairs
of underpants,

00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:20.406
a monkey wrench and 100-ounce
container of mustard.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.807
The agent asked me,
"Where are you going?"

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:24.677
And when I said LaGuardia,
he said, "This is JFK,"

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.579
to which I said, "I don't
remember how this works!"

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:29.716
I used to get to the airport
by the skin of my teeth

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.116
45 minutes
before takeoff,

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.453
just enough time to skate
through pre-check,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.688
chug a Bloody Mary at the bar
next to the Hudson News

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:39.058
and then by the coldest
chef salad ever made

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.561
at a Fridays To Go, you know,
ham chunks like ice cubes.

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.864
Now I'm so desperate
to get out of the house,

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.833
I show up four hours early
and get so bored

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:50.202
I end up browsing those luggage
stores at the airport,

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:54.207
which I've never understood,
who shows up to the airport

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.108
needing luggage.

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.578
"Hey, you got anything I can put
all these clothes in?"

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.247
An airport
trying to sell you luggage

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.016
is like Taco Bell
trying to sell you weed.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:07.720
"Oh, yeah, we're good,
Taco Bell.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.022
We, like,
already thought of that."

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:11.724
I'm not the only one

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.792
reacquainting myself
with travel etiquette.

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:17.363
Remember when Rudy Giuliani got
caught shaving in an airport?

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:21.567
-Rudy Giuliani was caught
using an electric shaver --

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.735
okay -- out in public
at the airport.

00:03:23.735 --> 00:03:25.137
But here's the thing,

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:27.840
he was sitting at the table
eating while he did it!

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.276
So Jeanne Moos shows you,
a guy who saw him,

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.612
had to get it on video,
and now millions see it.

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.048
-First, he had lobster bisque.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.017
Then he began grooming.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:41.020
-Stars -- they're just like
none of us.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.122
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.357
Yeah, they really happened --
this dingus used to be the mayor

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:46.926
of New York
and personal attorney

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.861
to the president
of the United States.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.997
And now he's at Pat LaFrieda's
in Terminal B,

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.265
getting chin hairs
all over his table.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.334
"Excuse me, waiter,
there's hair in my soup!

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.435
I demand a refund!"

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.704
"Well, you are shaving."
"Fair point;

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:00.806
what do you say
we go halvsies?"

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.008
And not only
have people forgotten

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.409
how to act in airports,

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.010
the same is true on airplanes

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.445
because suffice it to say,

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:08.581
it's been a rough year
for the friendly skies.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.584
-The newest problem facing
pent-up demand for travel

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.919
is pent-up frustrations
in the sky,

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:17.122
with federal agencies
citing a serious surge

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:19.091
of in-flight fights.

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:21.227
-The number of fights
between passengers

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.161
and airline workers
are on the rise.

00:04:23.161 --> 00:04:26.599
-We've had to deal with
almost riot like incidences.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.569
-Fist fights, drinking, verbally
and physically assaulting

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.736
flight attendants.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:33.472
2,500 cases so far this year.

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:38.277
-2,500 reports already from
the airlines of passengers

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:42.247
engaging in fights, arguing over
the masks, drinking.

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:44.517
-Damn. I mean, usually when
I get drunk on a plane,

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.585
I just pass out watching a movie
I've never heard of,

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.454
like "Naughty Grandpa"
or "Crazy Christmas,"

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.323
starring Owen Wilson
as a college dropout

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.391
who gets hired to be
the real Santa Claus.

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:54.660
"We got to make
all these toys ourselves?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:58.463
Gee whiz, man.
Wow! Wow!"

00:04:58.463 --> 00:05:02.635
And just to be clear,
now that an audience is back,

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.004
I will not be doing
my Vince Vaughn impression.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.073
Truth be tro--
truth be told,

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.740
I just don't have the confidence

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.644
to do it
in front of people.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.946
Although, you know,
if Vince Vaughn were here...

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.615
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:19.785
I feel like he'd probably
say something like, uh...

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:22.855
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.590
"Buddy, buddy, buddy,
what are you talking about?

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.560
That impression is money!
Seriously, though..."

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.664
Oh boy.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:34.534
"How'd it go?"
They applauded before.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:38.537
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.472
Seriously, though,
what is wrong with people?

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.341
Flying is stressful enough
without drinking,

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.542
fist fights and riots.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.044
Air travel is turning into
a soccer match

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.112
at Wembley Stadium --
one time, I accidentally

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:48.781
cut a dude in line
and he screamed,

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.718
"You [bleep] wanker,"
and then head-butted me.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:54.186
Then he bought me a pint; point
in soccer's a weird sport.

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:55.587
Things are getting
so out of hand,

00:05:55.587 --> 00:05:58.224
United just added a section
after first class and coach

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.125
that's just an MMA style octagon

00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:02.561
and your boarding pass
looks like this.

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:04.597
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.966
[ Laughing ]
The point is...

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.301
We should have gone with
the Old Scottish Detective --

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:13.039
we should call back
that gold!

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:16.275
Once again, if you're watching
"A Closer Look" online,

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.543
wait eight hours

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:20.379
and then watch the monologue
that we post later,

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.281
and then you'll get
that sweet callback

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.217
to Old Scottish Detective.

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:27.019
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.354
The point is, air travel

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.089
has already been
bad enough this year,

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.792
but over the weekend it got even
worse for thousands of travelers

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:35.494
who are stranded thanks to a
meltdown at Southwest Airlines.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:37.696
-The travel nightmare
for thousands of passengers

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.098
after Southwest Airlines

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:42.100
canceled more than 2,200 flights
in just the past three days.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.104
Stranded passengers again today,
hours-long lines

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:48.241
at the Denver airport
just to reschedule flights.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.576
-About 90 more flights
canceled today

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.579
as Southwest Airlines struggles
to get back to normal

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.048
after days of chaos
and cancelations.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.651
-Tonight, travel chaos
and confusion.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.554
Southwest Airlines
cancels thousands of flights,

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:03.656
leaving passengers stranded.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.659
Lines were long and tempers
were short at airports

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:09.728
in several cities as passengers
were forced to wait hours

00:07:09.728 --> 00:07:11.931
and in some cases, days --

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.467
yes, days --
to get on other flights.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:17.336
-Can you imagine waiting days
to reschedule a flight?

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.104
That's not rescheduling anymore?

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:21.674
You just live
in the airport now.

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.409
"Welcome to Cinnabon.
What can I get you?"

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.210
"I don't know,
a job application?"

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.779
I'm just kidding.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:30.416
No one has ever said "Welcome
to Cinnabon" at an airport.

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:34.487
The best you're going to get is,
"Let me guess -- 2?!"

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:36.588
And it's especially bad
for Southwest

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:37.890
because a lot
of their passengers

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.759
are flying to places
like Florida on vacation.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.426
It'd be one thing
if you were stuck in the airport

00:07:41.426 --> 00:07:42.662
on your way to a business trip,

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:44.730
but if you're going to Disney
with your family

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:45.898
and you're three days late?

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.433
"All right, everyone,
we made it.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.134
We got 45 minutes
inside the park,

00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:50.502
then we got to turn
around and go home.

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:52.905
Why don't you kids go wait in
line at Space Mountain

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.007
while your mother and I
go get divorced?"

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:59.011
Now, the company, the pilots'
union and the FAA

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.413
have all attributed
the chaos to various factors,

00:08:01.413 --> 00:08:03.282
from weather
to air traffic control

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.317
to antiquated
scheduling technology.

00:08:05.317 --> 00:08:08.387
The airline and the president
of the Southwest Pilots' Union

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:11.123
have said repeatedly
the meltdown has nothing,

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:12.724
nothing to do
with vaccine mandates,

00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:14.493
but that hasn't stopped some
on the right

00:08:14.493 --> 00:08:16.294
from spreading
the baseless claim anyway.

00:08:16.294 --> 00:08:18.697
-Some congressional Republicans
said it's a sick-out

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:20.833
in response
to the vaccine mandates.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.367
Arizona Congressman Andy Biggs

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:25.304
tweeted, "I stand with Southwest
Airlines employees

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.372
who are fighting
against these mandates."

00:08:27.372 --> 00:08:29.375
The union president
for Southwest pilots

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.543
told Fox News
there is no sick-out.

00:08:31.543 --> 00:08:33.779
These issues are because
of poor management."

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:36.214
-Senator Ted Cruz blaming
President Joe Biden's

00:08:36.214 --> 00:08:38.950
"illegal vaccine mandate"
for the shortage."

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.386
-We can tell you that the
shutdown of Southwest Airlines

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:44.056
over the weekend
was a direct consequence --

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:47.926
it was a reaction to Joe Biden's
vaccine mandates.

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:50.329
There were more cancelations
at Southwest Airlines today;

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.697
no doubt there'll be
more to come --

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.899
and not just of airline flights.

00:08:53.899 --> 00:08:56.435
At least two Amtrak train routes
in the Northeast

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.070
were canceled over the weekend,

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.073
and so is a regularly scheduled
car ferry in Washington state

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:03.175
out to the San Juan Islands.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:06.445
In all cases, the employees
in question who have been told

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.348
to get the shot did not show up.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:13.285
Were these also protests
against the Biden shot mandates?

00:09:13.285 --> 00:09:14.586
We can't say for certain.

00:09:14.586 --> 00:09:16.289
It certainly wouldn't
surprise us.

00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:17.523
-You can't say for certain?!

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:19.491
Well, then, please,
by all means,

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:20.659
put it on television.

00:09:20.659 --> 00:09:22.461
We all know
that's how journalism works.

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:25.063
Who can forget the famous
Woodward and Bernstein headline

00:09:25.063 --> 00:09:26.365
"Did Nixon do Watergate?

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:30.002
Seems like the kind of thing
he'd do! But who knows?"

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:32.838
I'll just never, personally,

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:36.008
I'll never tire of Tucker's
just-asking-questions routine.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:39.111
"Where are these protests
against Biden's vaccine mandate?

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:41.947
Did Joe Biden secretly replace
all the real pilots

00:09:41.947 --> 00:09:43.849
with communists,
antifa woke-inistas?

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:47.119
Or we're the delays caused
because the flight attendants

00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:49.754
refuse to give you a second bag
of Biscoff cookies

00:09:49.754 --> 00:09:51.290
when you ask for one,

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.425
because, according to them,
the plane was taking off soon.

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:55.227
And when they asked you
to put up your tray table,

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:57.796
you said no because you still
had one Biscoff cookie left

00:09:57.796 --> 00:10:00.332
that you were saving for later,
and if you put it in your lap,

00:10:00.332 --> 00:10:02.368
you'd get crumbs on
your nicest travel slacks.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:04.537
And when they threatened
to remove you from the plane

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:06.405
and you said it was your
God-given right

00:10:06.405 --> 00:10:07.673
under Article 67, sections C,

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:09.274
of the
United States Constitution,

00:10:09.274 --> 00:10:12.411
part 9, to do what you wanted
with your Biscoff cookie,

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:13.679
the guy next to you said

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.081
loud enough for everyone
on the plane to hear,

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:18.417
'Biscoff? More like jerk off!'
and everyone laughed.

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:20.219
Even the pilots laughed

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:22.421
because you can hear them
chuckling over the intercom.

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:24.023
And when you then lie down
in the aisle

00:10:24.023 --> 00:10:26.358
as means of protest and scream,
'I'm not moving

00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:28.761
until everyone on this plane
gets unvaccinated,'

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:31.697
only to be told that wasn't
possible, then you yell,

00:10:31.697 --> 00:10:33.331
'It is possible,
you can poop it out,

00:10:33.331 --> 00:10:35.634
I read it on Facebook,'
but before you could provide

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:37.435
the link
for everyone to read,

00:10:37.435 --> 00:10:39.571
did a large man lift you up
and shove you into

00:10:39.571 --> 00:10:41.606
the overhead compartment
while everyone cheered?

00:10:41.606 --> 00:10:44.176
Could that be why the plane
was delayed?

00:10:44.176 --> 00:10:47.245
Well, we can tell you
that it is.

00:10:47.245 --> 00:10:49.180
Because it happened
to me yesterday."

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:51.584
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:53.486
And that wasn't
the only example --

00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:56.254
another show on Fox found a way
to tie it all the way back

00:10:56.254 --> 00:10:57.756
to -- what else?
The war on Christmas.

00:10:57.756 --> 00:11:01.059
-The left's war on Christmas
could continue with delays

00:11:01.059 --> 00:11:03.428
and shortages of pilots
right around the holidays.

00:11:03.428 --> 00:11:05.263
-Yeah. Mayor Pete's going
to have his hands full.

00:11:05.263 --> 00:11:06.698
I mean, he is really in charge
of that.

00:11:06.698 --> 00:11:08.266
-Where is he, anyway?
-Where is Mayor Pete?

00:11:08.266 --> 00:11:09.902
If you have all
this labor action

00:11:09.902 --> 00:11:13.205
happening right before
the holidays, Christmas?

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.673
-Okay, first of all,
it's October,

00:11:14.673 --> 00:11:16.041
you don't get to start with
the war on Christmas yet.

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:17.376
We're still in the middle
of the war on Halloween.

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:18.744
I'm talking to you,
people with

00:11:18.744 --> 00:11:20.579
the motion-sensor skeletons
on their porches.

00:11:20.579 --> 00:11:22.147
When I walk my children
to school,

00:11:22.147 --> 00:11:23.282
they shouldn't have to hear
their father

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:24.784
yelp like a Chihuahua,
because he thinks

00:11:24.784 --> 00:11:26.518
an army of the undead
are coming for him.

00:11:26.518 --> 00:11:28.654
Plus, my kids
are still mad at me

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:29.955
for using them as human shields.

00:11:29.955 --> 00:11:32.124
"Take the boys!

00:11:32.124 --> 00:11:34.760
I have no quarrel with you,
Skeleton King!"

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.263
But seriously, Fox News,
take it one holiday at a time,

00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:39.431
at least come up with a fake
conspiracy theory

00:11:39.431 --> 00:11:41.667
about Halloween first --
"The left wants to cancel

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:44.236
Jack-o-lanterns, faces are too
scary for their snowflakes,

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:45.937
so now they've changed
the name of Halloween

00:11:45.937 --> 00:11:48.440
to All Gourds Day."

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.377
Also -- true story -- I ordered
a pirate costume online

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:54.046
for my son to trick or treat in,
and they emailed back saying,

00:11:54.046 --> 00:11:55.847
"Should be there by
October 28th.

00:11:55.847 --> 00:11:57.917
What's the date of your event?"

00:11:57.917 --> 00:11:59.919
[ Laughter ]

00:11:59.919 --> 00:12:01.787
What's the date?

00:12:01.787 --> 00:12:04.222
I need a pirate costume
for a three year old --

00:12:04.222 --> 00:12:06.659
"Oh, uh, November 23,
we celebrate

00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:08.727
Swashbuckler Thanksgiving!"

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:10.662
Again, both the airline

00:12:10.662 --> 00:12:12.598
and the president
of Southwest Pilots' Union

00:12:12.598 --> 00:12:14.767
have said repeatedly
that the Southwest meltdown

00:12:14.767 --> 00:12:16.534
had nothing to do
with the vaccine mandate.

00:12:16.534 --> 00:12:19.705
In fact, the president
of the Southwest Pilots' Union

00:12:19.705 --> 00:12:21.973
said it on Fox News.

00:12:21.973 --> 00:12:23.776
-Seeing a lot of people
invested in this idea

00:12:23.776 --> 00:12:28.046
that this is somehow related
to vaccine mandates.

00:12:28.046 --> 00:12:29.748
-There's just
no evidence of that.

00:12:29.748 --> 00:12:32.785
-You say it was not an issue,
but to what degree

00:12:32.785 --> 00:12:36.188
did it contribute
to this problem at all?

00:12:36.188 --> 00:12:38.356
-Zero.
-You're saying

00:12:38.356 --> 00:12:40.058
this was not
because of a sick-out.

00:12:40.058 --> 00:12:42.794
This was not an organized
job action,

00:12:42.794 --> 00:12:46.131
had nothing to do yet
with the vaccine mandate.

00:12:46.131 --> 00:12:49.367
-Absolutely not, the two
are mutually exclusive.

00:12:49.367 --> 00:12:51.837
What we've seen now
that we're at Monday

00:12:51.837 --> 00:12:53.839
and looking back at the data,

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:56.075
our pilots' sick rates
were right in line

00:12:56.075 --> 00:12:58.944
with where
they were this summer.

00:12:58.944 --> 00:13:03.715
We also see our pilots picking
up even more than normal now.

00:13:03.715 --> 00:13:07.019
So our pilots are out there
serving our customers.

00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:09.021
They're out there
picking up extra time.

00:13:09.021 --> 00:13:12.291
So it is absolutely false
that our pilots

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:15.160
are engaged in any sort of
job action.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.162
-That last clip was on Fox News.

00:13:17.162 --> 00:13:18.831
I mean, do you guys even watch
your own network?

00:13:18.831 --> 00:13:20.365
That'd be like
if I came out here and said,

00:13:20.365 --> 00:13:23.802
"Chicago doesn't have fires!"

00:13:23.802 --> 00:13:25.904
Or if I said, "In the criminal
justice system,

00:13:25.904 --> 00:13:27.973
the people aren't represented
by two separate

00:13:27.973 --> 00:13:30.075
but equally important groups."
[ Double tone ]

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:31.844
Look --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:31.844 --> 00:13:34.779
It's especially rich for Fox
hosts to applaud employees

00:13:34.779 --> 00:13:37.616
standing up against vaccine
or testing requirements

00:13:37.616 --> 00:13:41.720
when their own company
has much stricter requirements.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:45.090
-Fox's vaccine policy actually
goes further than Biden's.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.492
Remember, Biden is calling
for weekly testing

00:13:47.492 --> 00:13:50.762
of many private sector workers
who don't get vaccinated.

00:13:50.762 --> 00:13:52.864
In a newly revealed
internal memo,

00:13:52.864 --> 00:13:56.001
Fox outlining a vaccine policy
that is stricter,

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:57.970
involving daily COVID testing.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:00.506
-Fox management is mandating
that employees

00:14:00.506 --> 00:14:03.108
disclose
their vaccination status.

00:14:03.108 --> 00:14:06.745
-Fox has a strict policy
of demanding all their workers

00:14:06.745 --> 00:14:10.081
be vaccinated
or face daily testing.

00:14:10.081 --> 00:14:12.685
90 percent of the FOX workforce

00:14:12.685 --> 00:14:15.487
reports that they are now
fully vaccinated.

00:14:15.487 --> 00:14:17.156
-That's right,
they have to get that swab

00:14:17.156 --> 00:14:18.556
shoved up their nose once a day.

00:14:18.556 --> 00:14:20.759
I'm vaxed, but I still get
tested three times a week,

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:22.595
and it sucks --
remember in the early days

00:14:22.595 --> 00:14:24.196
when they had to shove it
really far up

00:14:24.196 --> 00:14:25.798
and it made you cry?

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:27.566
One time they shoved the swab
so far up my nose,

00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:31.903
I forgot three years of college
and I had to get my degree back.

00:14:31.903 --> 00:14:33.939
The only swabbing I like
is when I use a roll

00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:36.041
to soak up the remaining gravy
on my plate.

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.509
during Swashbucklers
Thanksgiving --

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:39.244
we call it swabbing.

00:14:39.244 --> 00:14:43.348
And, yeah, when the first
Swashbucklers Thanksgiving joke

00:14:43.348 --> 00:14:44.716
didn't work great,

00:14:44.716 --> 00:14:46.851
I was aware...

00:14:46.851 --> 00:14:48.987
I was aware that a callback
was coming,

00:14:48.987 --> 00:14:53.626
and there was no way
to get out of it.

00:14:53.626 --> 00:14:56.294
This is this sort
of new gambling you do

00:14:56.294 --> 00:14:57.829
with an audience.

00:14:57.829 --> 00:15:03.702
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:03.702 --> 00:15:06.672
I hope it was worth it
for all you people at home!

00:15:09.007 --> 00:15:10.709
The hypocrisy here is brazen,

00:15:10.709 --> 00:15:12.010
and it's something
that President Biden

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.312
seems to enjoy pointing out,
as he did last week.

00:15:14.312 --> 00:15:19.985
-Even -- this I always get
a kick out of -- Fox News!

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:24.956
Fox News requires vaccinations
for all employees.

00:15:24.956 --> 00:15:27.059
Give me a break.
Fox News.

00:15:27.059 --> 00:15:30.895
-Oh, damn, he busted out
the Biden whisper.

00:15:30.895 --> 00:15:33.132
The one where he sounds
like he's doing ASMR.

00:15:33.132 --> 00:15:34.967
Next time he does that,
he should crinkle a bag

00:15:34.967 --> 00:15:36.635
of potato chips.

00:15:36.635 --> 00:15:39.271
[ Crinkling ]
"Even Fox News requires

00:15:39.271 --> 00:15:41.839
vaccination
of all their employees.

00:15:41.839 --> 00:15:44.709
Crisp, cringley crackers,

00:15:44.709 --> 00:15:47.746
crackling cranky crazies."

00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:50.649
Biden wasn't
entirely precise there.

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:54.118
Fox requires employers to report
their vaccination status,

00:15:54.118 --> 00:15:56.488
and if they're not vaccinated,
they get tested daily.

00:15:56.488 --> 00:15:59.925
Biden's policy is to get
vaccinated or get tested weekly.

00:15:59.925 --> 00:16:02.394
So Fox's policy
is actually stricter.

00:16:02.394 --> 00:16:04.430
And yet Republican politicians
across the country

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.364
have decided to rail
against vaccine mandates.

00:16:06.364 --> 00:16:08.833
You know what would really
ruin the holidays?

00:16:08.833 --> 00:16:10.035
Another COVID spike.

00:16:10.035 --> 00:16:12.204
Oh, my God, does that...

00:16:12.204 --> 00:16:13.705
Does that mean Republicans are
part of the --

00:16:13.705 --> 00:16:14.907
-War on Christmas.

00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:16.808
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

